  {
   "text": "{\"sections\":[{\"section\":\"summary\",\"body\":\"Harrowgate Precision Components reported higher earnings and lower debt for the twelve months ended September 30, 2026. Revenue rose to {{fact:f7d0e090-436a-4273-83ba-4a8ede62b72c}} from {{fact:86962410-1fa6-4eab-8a4d-94dff0641899}}, and total debt to EBITDA declined to {{fact:32cac748-8985-4064-9da8-d8d05c11cf2c}} from {{fact:722db283-6633-40ec-a4e3-3524bf00316a}}. All tested covenants were met, and the compliance certificate agrees with the bank's calculations. The borrowing base agrees, with availability of {{fact:3f808d51-2537-4682-874a-37dc8c7217b7}}. No early warning signals fired and no items are awaiting a decision.\"},{\"section\":\"performance\",\"body\":\"Trailing twelve month revenue increased to {{fact:f7d0e090-436a-4273-83ba-4a8ede62b72c}} from {{fact:86962410-1fa6-4eab-8a4d-94dff0641899}}, growth of {{fact:517461f8-6a11-497e-85df-59bd949c94ad}}. EBITDA rose to {{fact:29a8e0cf-2c70-440c-a5b0-33c60c35fa01}} from {{fact:b8fbee20-c5d7-4c59-b104-88a3bec69bfa}}. The EBITDA margin was {{fact:8f0ad967-c739-47a0-81a9-4ebf18cac0fd}}, level with {{fact:614cebe2-c782-4fc4-89e0-ee801d2d7348}} a year earlier. Net income increased to {{fact:8dc750f9-d4cb-4660-a67d-b00f4b88543c}} from {{fact:34788b2a-3ebd-45d7-97e5-fc5900c7298c}}. Interest coverage improved to {{fact:8d6f921a-bff7-4b91-ab96-48287f6a538f}} from {{fact:a558ad29-c418-4f13-8201-594662c0b5a5}}. Total debt fell to {{fact:90c875dd-d22b-416f-b551-a8a9b9a79303}} from {{fact:212efe30-d51b-4a34-9199-c63f1ceb50b4}}, and cash rose to {{fact:01179cf4-f21f-4966-887b-d7d706f0a25c}} from {{fact:8e814dad-8f2f-4209-a3e7-3f6a7de4e480}}. Working capital was steady. The current ratio was {{fact:2cc9c89a-c415-46ee-8416-73af9eedd116}}, compared with {{fact:0f301368-ffdd-42b7-bd8d-1acd9f12718a}} a year earlier. DSO shortened to {{fact:107bb226-907a-4157-9c7a-6426d245e914}} from {{fact:ba5d5217-9bd1-4137-9dec-0e9cdeb6f516}}, and DPO shortened to {{fact:b75e1550-a052-43fe-8461-db74b19494f7}} from {{fact:a5043bcb-c057-4f07-9d24-8ab29c7aae89}}.\"},{\"section\":\"covenants\",\"body\":\"All covenants were compliant at September 30, 2026. In each case the certificate figure matches the bank's calculation. The Fixed Charge Coverage Ratio was {{fact:2e1f792a-e989-4a42-8067-b5b479e959b1}} against a minimum of {{fact:1eaf1d27-d9f7-40dc-baca-3e8abf377afa}}, a cushion of {{fact:b8c1384c-cda4-4f49-a680-8db8a67d2981}}. Tangible Net Worth was {{fact:20db4f2c-b2c8-423a-a1ac-fb32c578f39c}} against a minimum of {{fact:b22f206d-71d3-48f1-84e8-b4ae57611522}}, a cushion of {{fact:54deea32-c61c-4c4e-a168-5c323d791a34}}. The Total Leverage Ratio was {{fact:0589019c-994e-438e-a2ea-25ffb59e6e9a}} against a maximum of {{fact:5c7d8948-7015-4f21-876b-965f9f8c3bce}}, a cushion of {{fact:8c27d4cf-d53e-4206-8c9c-5bd35eedf80e}}. Leverage carries the narrowest cushion of the tested covenants.\"},{\"section\":\"collateral\",\"body\":\"The borrowing base supporting the Revolving Line of Credit was tested as of September 30, 2026. The borrower's certificate agrees with the bank's calculation, with no mismatched lines. Availability was {{fact:3f808d51-2537-4682-874a-37dc8c7217b7}}.\"},{\"section\":\"risks\",\"body\":\"No early warning signals fired this period, and there are no open work items awaiting review. Of the tested covenants, the Total Leverage Ratio has the smallest cushion, at {{fact:8c27d4cf-d53e-4206-8c9c-5bd35eedf80e}}. A reviewer may wish to note this as the covenant most sensitive to any decline in EBITDA.\"}]}",
   "type": "text"
  }
